# ==============================================================================
# OLIST NO-SQL PROJECT - ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# ==============================================================================
# 
# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file and rename it to ".env" in the root directory:
#    $ cp .env.example .env
# 
# 2. Retrieve your Kaggle API credentials:
#    a. Log into Kaggle (https://www.kaggle.com).
#    b. Go to your Account Settings page (https://www.kaggle.com/settings).
#    c. Scroll down to the "API" section and click "Create New Token".
#    d. A file named "kaggle.json" will download. Open it using a text editor.
# 
# 3. Copy the values of "username" and "key" from that file and paste them below:
#    (Note: Do NOT include quotes, spaces, or brackets around the values)
# 
# 4. Save the ".env" file. Docker Compose will automatically read this file
#    and inject these variables into the ETL container at runtime.
# 
# WARNING:
# Never commit your real ".env" file containing active secrets to Git!
# The ".env" file is already listed in the .gitignore to prevent accidental leaks.
# ==============================================================================

# Your Kaggle username (e.g., netanelrahum)
KAGGLE_USERNAME=your_kaggle_username

# Your 32-character Kaggle API key (e.g., 92b79f5d1dcaed94264297c61bde1dc7)
KAGGLE_KEY=your_kaggle_key
